; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Maryland remains one of the most Democratic states in presidential voting, with a partisan lean of roughly fifteen points toward Democrats and Democratic nominees carrying it by double digits in every recent cycle. No general-election polls or expert ratings are available for this race, so the estimate rests on the state's underlying partisan balance.\n\nThe open-seat nature of the contest adds little either way, since Maryland's presidential vote has tracked its lean regardless of incumbency. The main uncertainty is the national environment: a strong Republican year could pull the margin toward single digits, while a Democratic-favorable climate could push it well past twenty points. Current headlines from the state center on downballot primaries and redistricting, with no sign of a presidential-level contest that would alter the state's basic alignment.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9506, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9102, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9258, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9194, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9194, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9136, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9144, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9103, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9184, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9155, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9262, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.91, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9155, "margin": 15.0}]}